
==============================================================================
1. Refused before solving: one reason, one pointer, one message
==============================================================================
  a valid order
    HTTP 200  {"status": "feasible", "boxes": 1, "left_out": []}
  quantity 0
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "below_minimum", "field": "/items/0/quantity", "message": "Please check item \"mug\", quantity: must be at least 1."}
  a negative width
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "negative_measure", "field": "/items/1/dimensions/width", "message": "Please check item \"teapot\", dimensions/width: cannot be negative."}
  a missing height
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "missing_field", "field": "/items/1/dimensions/height", "message": "Please check item \"teapot\", dimensions/height: is required."}
  a float where a measure belongs
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "wrong_type", "field": "/items/1/dimensions/width", "message": "Please check item \"teapot\", dimensions/width: must be a measure."}
  the same container id twice
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "duplicate_id", "field": "/containers/1/id", "message": "Please check container \"box\", id: repeats the id \"box\"."}
  an unknown solver profile
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_request", "reason": "not_allowed", "field": "/configuration/solver_profile", "message": "Please check /configuration/solver_profile: must be one of [\"fast\",\"balanced\",\"quality\",\"exact_small\"]."}

  A float is refused as a measure on purpose: binary floating point cannot hold most
  decimal lengths exactly, and every length here is exact. Send "160.5" as a string.
  When several values are wrong, the first is reported, in a fixed order every
  engine shares: units, configuration, items, containers, fixed placements.

==============================================================================
2. Items already in place that cannot be there
==============================================================================
  a teapot already in the box, packed around
    HTTP 200  {"status": "feasible", "boxes": 1, "left_out": []}
  a teapot recorded at x = 200 mm, hanging out of a 300 mm box
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_fixed_placement", "reason": "cannot_hold", "field": "/fixed_placements", "message": "The items already loaded cannot stay as recorded: outside_container: teapot#1."}
  a mug and the teapot recorded in the same place
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_fixed_placement", "reason": "cannot_hold", "field": "/fixed_placements", "message": "The items already loaded cannot stay as recorded: collision: teapot#1 with mug#1."}
  an orientation code that does not exist
    HTTP 422  {"code": "invalid_fixed_placement", "reason": "malformed", "field": "/fixed_placements/0/orientation", "message": "The items already loaded cannot stay as recorded: fixed_placements[0].orientation is one of the six codes."}

  `cannot_hold` means the fixed set is well formed but is not a valid packing on its
  own, and `field` is the whole list. `malformed` points at the one bad value.

==============================================================================
3. Not an error: a valid order that does not fit
==============================================================================
  a teapot too tall for any box
    HTTP 200  {"status": "best_found", "boxes": 1, "left_out": ["teapot#1"]}

  The caller asked a fair question and got an answer: the rest of the order is
  packed, and `unpacked_items` says what is not and why. Retrying it will not help,
  and neither will treating it as a 4xx.

==============================================================================
4. Two refusals that do not carry a pointer
==============================================================================
  an unknown objective: InvalidRequestError
  an unknown door: InvalidRequestError

  Both are `ValueError`s, so a handler that ends with `except ValueError` still turns
  them into a 422 -- but they have no `reason` or `field` to highlight, only a message.
